        <!-- Closing CTA -->
        <div class="mt-16 bg-gray-900 text-white rounded-2xl p-8">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            <strong class="text-white">Run tall, look ahead, land under your hips, swing your
            arms and keep off the rails.</strong> If you overstride, take slightly quicker steps —
            a few percent above your natural cadence, not a leap to 180.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Do not force a forefoot strike, change one thing at a time, and film yourself side-on to
            see what is really happening. The belt does not run for you; the basics of getting on
